  "format": "gai-icon/2",
  "id": "reduced-motion",
  "label": "Reduced motion",
  "intent": "The ball brakes and its motion trails die down. Light: the ball lurches forward as it brakes and rocks back into place, while the three trails behind it retract to short stubs one after another, top to bottom, each snapping a little short and settling. Strong: the ball pumps the brakes twice, and the trails shrink in two steps, half way, then down to the stubs. The stubs hold; the reverse lets the trails stream out again.",
